feat(benchmark): add the small-state scenario and the break-even rule

The corpus only had scenarios with a large state, so restating the evidence
always cost more than the deliberation it removed and the report could not say
where the crossover is. A fifth scenario routes a one-line request through the
shipped request bank, which is the shape the plugin is actually for.

Measured against the live API, that scenario still loses on raw tokens (-35.3%
in the bank shape) because TypeSafe bills a rubric far above what four
characters per token predicts. What the data does support is now stated
exactly: the bank shape breaks even at an output weight of 2.7, above which Jev
is cheaper, and the ad-hoc shape never breaks even at any weight because the
agent generates the questions itself.

The modelled run now also reports the estimator's error against measurement:
four characters per token under-counts Jev's billed input by about 1.6x on this
corpus.
